+# Task: Termux follow-ups — `apt` install kind in `indus update`, `validate` stage in the Termux build (W50 slice d) Phase: follow-ups Owner: wave-50 builder d
+
+## Status
+
+Done (2026-10-23), on the host side. Built and tested here: the `apt` install kind and its Termux
+refusal in `indus update` (`-y`, `--check`, `--channel`, `--plan`), `repo.py validate` / `repo.py
+sign` (and validation before signing in the one-call `build --key-file`), and `build.sh`'s
+`repo` → `validate` → `sign` stages, run end to end with fake docker / git / uv and the real
+`dpkg-deb`. Never run here (no docker, no aarch64, placeholder digest): the real lane, and the
+install / upgrade proof in a Termux container (still owed, see "Left out"). Outside the slice's own
+files: a short pointer section in `docs/notes/P24/termux.md`; the fake `.deb` helper in
+`tests/unit/release/test_termux_repo.py` now lays out the Termux payload (the existing tests sign,
+so their packages must validate).
+
+Read (reference @ `ab3fe9dffb0a89d534cb795e2a2940e5f6542056`): `hermes_cli/config.py` (the install-method
+stamp set and the per-method update command: `apt` is the Termux channel by contract),
+`hermes_cli/web_routers/actions.py` (the `apt` refusal line only), `scripts/termux/validate_installed.py`
+(what the installed-package proof checks, incl. the updater refusal), `scripts/termux/check_apt.sh`
+and `check_deb.sh` (the in-container install proofs), `scripts/termux/stage_apt_repo.py` (skim: what it
+checks before signing — the control fields only). Ours: `docs/notes/P24/termux.md` (W49-c-8 and the
+"Not taken" validate follow-up), `scripts/termux/build.sh`, `scripts/termux/repo.py`,
+`src/indus/cli/update/__init__.py`, `src/indus/cli/version.py`, `docs/user/getting-started/install.md`
+(Termux section). Closed before writing.
+Evidence: none (CLI message and packaging script; no running reference needed).
+
+What it does (own words):
+- `indus update` on a copy installed from the Termux APT channel (its `.install_method` stamp says
+  `apt`, written by `build.sh`) now knows that kind by name: it is refused like the other installs a
+  package manager owns, with the one instruction that works there — `pkg upgrade indus-agent` — and
+  never tries to move the tree itself. Before, the unknown stamp fell through to `package` and
+  told a phone user to reinstall with install.sh, which refuses Termux.
+- The Termux build gets a `validate` stage between assembling the repository and signing it. The
+  repository is first written unsigned, then `repo.py validate` checks the tree: the Release names
+  exactly the two indexes with the right sizes and SHA-256, `Packages.gz` holds the same bytes as
+  `Packages`, every stanza points at a pool file of the stated size and digest whose control
+  matches the stanza, the tag's version is listed, and the tag's package has the on-device layout
+  (everything under the Termux prefix, an executable `bin/indus`, the venv's python, the app's
+  `src/indus/__init__.py`, and the `.install_method` stamp saying `apt` — the stamp the updater
+  relies on). Only then does `repo.py sign` sign it. A tree that fails is never signed.
+
+Inputs → outputs:
+- `.install_method` = `apt` → `detect_kind` = `apt`; `indus update` (any of `-y`, `--check`) exit 1
+  with the Termux message; `--plan` → `install_kind: apt`, `action: refused`, `reason` = message.
+- `repo.py validate --out DIR --tag TAG` → exit 0 (prints the suite and count), 4 with one line per
+  problem, 2 on bad arguments / tag.
+- `repo.py sign --out DIR --tag TAG [--key-file F]` → validates first (4, nothing signed), then 3
+  unsigned without a key or gpg, 0 signed (InRelease, Release.gpg, key.asc).
+- `repo.py build ... --key-file F` (one call) validates before it signs too.
+- `build.sh` stages: `... pack repo validate sign` (11); `repo` must end unsigned (exit 3), any
+  other code stops the build; `validate` failure → exit 4; `sign` passes its 0 / 3 through.
+
+Files: `src/indus/cli/update/__init__.py`, `scripts/termux/repo.py`, `scripts/termux/build.sh`,
+`tests/unit/cli/update/test_channels.py`, `tests/unit/cli/commands/test_update.py`,
+`tests/unit/release/test_termux_repo.py`, `tests/unit/release/test_termux_build_script.py`,
+`docs/notes/P24/termux.md` (pointer), this note.
+
+Edge cases / failure modes:
+- `apt` stamp with different case or a BOM → the version module already lower-cases and strips.
+- A checkout with `.git` and an `apt` stamp is still `apt` (the stamp wins; the package manager owns
+  the tree).
+- Release missing, a third index named, an index missing or edited after the Release was written,
+  a name that climbs out (`..`) → problems, exit 4.
+- `Packages.gz` not gzip, or not the same bytes → problem; its decompression is bounded.
+- Stanza missing Filename/Size/SHA256, a Filename that is not the pool path the control fields give,
+  pool file missing / wrong size / wrong digest, a pool `.deb` whose control disagrees → problems.
+- The tag's version not listed → problem (validating the wrong suite or a failed assembly).
+- Payload: an entry outside the Termux prefix or with `..`, no `bin/indus` or not executable, no
+  stamp or a stamp that is not `apt`, no venv python, no app package → problems.
+- `sign` on a tree never assembled → exit 4 (Release missing), nothing written.
+
+Our design differences / decisions:
+- **W50-d-1** The message names the real package, `indus-agent` (`pkg upgrade indus-agent`, as the
+  install guide already says); the brief's `pkg upgrade indus` would not find a package.
+- **W50-d-2** `apt` is the Termux channel by contract (the only producer of that stamp is
+  `scripts/termux/build.sh`), so the refusal speaks about Termux and `pkg`. Exit 1 like the other
+  managed kinds (the reference's validation expects its own exit 2; ours keeps one code for every
+  refusal).
+- **W50-d-3** Signing moves out of the `repo` stage: `repo` assembles unsigned (exit 3 is its
+  success), `validate` checks, `sign` signs (new `repo.py sign`). `repo.py build --key-file` keeps
+  doing both in one call and runs the same validation before signing, so no path signs an
+  unchecked tree.
+- **W50-d-4** New exit code 4 for "the built repository is invalid", apart from 2 (bad input) and
+  3 (unsigned), so CI logs say which. Problems are collected, not first-only.
+- **W50-d-5** Every listed package's pool file is checked by size and digest; only the tag's own
+  package is opened for the payload layout (older versions were checked when they were added).
+- Left out: the in-container install / upgrade proof (dpkg + apt in a Termux rootfs, the reference's
+  `check_apt.sh` role) — it needs docker and an aarch64 host; follow-up for the first lane run.
+  `indus uninstall` and the dashboard's update hint keep their current handling of `apt`
+  (follow-ups, not this slice).
+
+Tests we will write:
+- `detect_kind` → `apt` from the stamp (also with `.git` present); `REFUSALS["apt"]` names `pkg upgrade
+  indus-agent`; the command refuses with it for `-y` and `--check`, and `--plan` says refused / apt.
+- `validate`: a good tree passes; each broken-tree case is reported (parametrised); the payload
+  cases; exit codes through `main`.
+- `sign`: refuses an invalid tree (nothing written), exit 3 without a key, signs with a fake signer
+  path; `build_repository` with a signer refuses an invalid package before signing.
+- `build.sh`: dry-run order (11 stages); a full fake-tool run (docker / git / uv / uname shims, a
+  copy of the scripts with a non-placeholder digest, the real `dpkg-deb` when present) reaches
+  `repo`, `validate`, `sign` in order, the real `.deb` passes validation and the run ends 3
+  (unsigned); a package without its stamp stops at `validate` with exit 4 and no signature.
+
+## Decisions for the lead
+- W50-d-1 (package name in the message), W50-d-3 (stage split, `repo.py sign`), W50-d-4 (exit 4).
+
+Compare checklist (filled after the rewrite; reopened `hermes_cli/config.py` (stamp set, update
+command map), `hermes_cli/web_routers/actions.py` (apt refusal), `scripts/termux/validate_installed.py`,
+`check_apt.sh`, `check_deb.sh`, `stage_apt_repo.py`):
+- [x] `apt` means the Termux channel by contract; the instruction is `pkg upgrade <package>` (test:
+      `tests/unit/cli/update/test_channels.py::test_the_termux_stamp_is_its_own_kind`)
+- [x] The updater refuses an `apt` install with that instruction and runs nothing (test:
+      `tests/unit/cli/commands/test_update.py::test_termux_install_is_sent_to_pkg`)
+- [x] The installed-package proof asserts the install method reads `apt`: ours checks the stamp
+      inside the `.deb` before signing instead (test:
+      `tests/unit/release/test_termux_repo.py::test_the_payload_layout_is_checked`,
+      `::test_nothing_is_signed_when_the_package_is_not_laid_out_for_termux`)
+- [x] The reference checks only control fields before signing; ours validates the whole suite
+      (tests: `test_termux_repo.py::test_a_damaged_tree_is_reported` (13 cases),
+      `::test_the_tags_version_must_be_listed`, `::test_an_assembled_tree_validates`,
+      `::test_sign_validates_then_signs`, `::test_real_gpg_signs_and_verifies[build-validate-sign]`)
+- [x] Stage order and the stop before signing (tests:
+      `tests/unit/release/test_termux_build_script.py::test_dry_run_lists_the_stages_in_order`,
+      `::test_the_host_half_validates_before_it_signs`,
+      `::test_a_package_that_fails_validation_is_never_signed`)
+- [x] Gap: a stamp written with a BOM or in capitals — read the same way in both places (tests:
+      `test_the_termux_stamp_is_its_own_kind`, `test_a_good_payload_has_no_problems`)
+- Deliberate differences: the reference's refusal exits 2, ours 1 like every managed kind
+  (W50-d-2); validation runs on the host from the archive, not by installing it (no docker here);
+  an `apt` stamp in a tree that also has `.git` is still `apt`.
+- Not taken: the reference's commit-build refusal (we publish no commit builds to the channel);
+  its by-hash index checks (we write no by-hash indexes); the dashboard / doctor hints for `apt`
+  and `indus uninstall`'s handling of it (follow-ups).
